6.2.evidence:
Part One
Regional Government Article 7 (1) The Regional Government in efforts to protect women is responsible for:
a. Guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. Establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women's rights;
c. Conducting cooperation with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of women's protection in accordance with laws and regulations;
d. Conducting rehabilitation and empowerment of women who are victims of violence;
e. Providing special protection to women victims of violence and human trafficking, and
f. Taking preventive actions in order to prevent violations of women's rights.
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by SKPD in accordance with their duties and functions.
